G54: USB serial console (MediaTek MUSB peripheral, boot-arg g54usb=1).

The G54's USB 2.0 controller is a MediaTek MUSB core ("mediatek,
mt6855-usb20", musb-hdrc) at 0x11210000, not ruby's MTU3, so ruby_usb.c
cannot drive it. bsd/dev/g54_usb.c is a small polled peripheral driver: one
kernel thread every 1 ms, PIO through the endpoint FIFOs, no IRQ, no
DMA/QMU. It presents a CDC-ACM function (Windows usbser, macOS AppleUSBCDC
and Linux cdc_acm bind without a driver install): EP1 bulk IN streams the
SWEET console log through sweet_log_copy(); opening the port (DTR) replays
the 4 MiB ring from its oldest byte, then follows it live. EP1 OUT is
drained and ignored.

Hardware facts from the stock 5-8-6 package (g54-xnu E42): clocks are
pericfg_ao 0x11036000 set/clr gates (clk-mt6855-peri.ko: usb_phy/usb_sys
bank 0 bits 30/31, usb_dma_bus/usb_mcu_bus bank 1 bits 0/1); the PHY is the
T-PHY v2 at 0x11e40000 (U2 bank +0x300, init as ruby_usb.c/mtk-tphy, board
eye values from the DT, device mode U2PHYDTM1 |= 0x202 as
phy-mtk-tphy.ko); VUSB is regulator-always-on. Status lines "G54 USB: ..."
every 5 s until the host configures it. Off by default.

